    "___CORRELATION - is made of co meaning \"together\" and Relation.\n",
    "- Two numerical column.\n",
    "- It helps to tell the two columns are redendant or not.\n",
    "- When two sets of data are strongly linked together we say they have a High Correlation.\n",
    "- It is positive if the value increases together and negative when only one value decreases and the other increases.\n",
    "- CORRELATION VALUES : -\n",
    "    1 is a perfect correlation.\n",
    "    0 is no correlation (the value dosent linked at all).[it is good]\n",
    "    -1 is a perfect negative correlation.\n",
    "- Correlation is not good with curves.\n",
    "- r is the correlation cofficient . it measurs the strength and direction of a linear relationship between two variables. it alwys falls between (-1 & 1). the sign indicates the direstion and while the absolute values indicates the strength of the association."
